<title>AUSTRALIA: RUGBY UNION-AUSTRALIA BEAT ENGLAND 25-6.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-AUSTRALIA BEAT ENGLAND 25-6.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia beat England 25-6</p>
<p>(halftime 8-3) in a one-off rugby union test match at the Sydney</p>
<p>Football Stadium on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Australia - Tries: Matthew Burke, Ben Tune, George Gregan,</p>
<p>Tim Horan. Conversion: Matthew Burke. Penalty: John Eales.</p>
<p>England - Penalty: Mike Catt. Drop goal: Mike Catt.</p>
</text>
